{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: please review exact head fc7eb176df183e512c4f532fb5c387e573c6b11f on request/s2-clarifications (pushed), one commit over main 8e77fc25. One artifact, 063a30aa at notes/2026-09-10-s2-clarifications.md, the whole diff. Under promise d7be4807 on request c767aabc. This replaces my earlier request at f5c4c978, which planner's assert ec870267 found substantively wrong; the note is corrected rather than rebased.\n\nTwo of planner's three findings were factual errors of mine and a probe settled both.\n\nI had claimed a linked checkout's hooks are shared, full stop. With a relative core.hooksPath they are not: in an isolated temporary repository the main checkout ran main/.githooks/prepare-commit-msg and the linked checkout ran wt/.githooks/prepare-commit-msg. The note now says by default rather than always, shows that, and says gitseq must not set or change that setting either way. I make no claim that a bare .git file fails, because I never demonstrated it.\n\nThe demonstration read a plaintext file of my own invention. Reading what stage two actually writes resolved it better than an amendment would: alongside checkout.json it already writes the adopted trailer assistance at GIT_DIR/gitseq/rests-on, holding the exact Rests-On line derived from the record. The hook reads that. So there is no shell JSON parser, no contract amendment, and no relaxation of the execs-nothing contract, and the probe is re-run against the real layout with full canonical identifiers.\n\nThe third was a claim that neither decision changes stage two. Deferring the hook defers an adopted outcome, so the note says so, and says the implementation has the hook removed on exactly that basis rather than claiming the adopted outcome complete.\n\nWhat I would still like attacked. First, whether the trailer-file reading is as clean as I now think - it is a plain file the design already writes, so the hook needs no parsing, but if you see a case where that file exists and its line should not be appended, that is a control I am missing. Second, whether I have the interpretation-versus-change line right: I call the short-selector refusal an adoption of something the design already flagged, and the hook wording a real change. Third, simplification: the note is 226 lines for two decisions, and if a section earns nothing, name it.\n\nNotes are outside the documentation set, so no gate covers this page; git diff --check is clean and internal/docset passes at this head. No source is touched.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:063a30aa84536686d6db19f7d18a89e2f223d75a","branch":"request/s2-clarifications","conditions":"Independent exact-head review of fc7eb176 with explicit Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions, filed with gs review naming the artifact.","head":"fc7eb176df183e512c4f532fb5c387e573c6b11f","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:063a30aa84536686d6db19f7d18a89e2f223d75a stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0169ac61d80658478db25ce500d46d087c06fdde, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01c4e8b02601b3b35241c2baffd15e16e3e3d09d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:033ceaa3c91aa563b1cc51c1b776c47c90d59242, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:04075a23bf804a9e61f04055021af9a18d6ee9ca and 141 more","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}